data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"cause_title","type":"template","content":"IN THE COURT OF DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE\n\nCriminal Miscellaneous Case No. _____ of 2026\n\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n\nRajan Kumar\nS/o Shri Mohan Kumar\nAge: 32 years\nR/o Village Danapur, District Patna, Bihar\n                                              ... Applicant\n\nVersus\n\nState of Bihar through the District Magistrate / S.P., Patna\n                                              ... Opposite Party","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"application_heading","type":"template","content":"APPLICATION FOR Regular Bail UNDER SECTION 480 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"addressing_clause","type":"template","content":"TO,\nTHE HONOURABLE DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE,\nPatna\n\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15.03.2026, registered at Police Station Kotwali, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and seeks regular bail in the aforesaid matter.\n\n2. That the Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the aforesaid FIR due to a pre-existing land dispute with the complainant. The allegations leveled against the Applicant are entirely baseless and motivated by malice and vendetta arising out of civil disputes between the parties.\n\n3. That the Applicant respectfully submits that he was not present at the time and place of the alleged incident and has credible witnesses who can establish his alibi beyond any shadow of doubt. The Applicant was arrested on 16.03.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then without any justifiable cause.\n\n4. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to personal animosity and civil disputes with the complainant. The allegations are completely fabricated and the Applicant is being made a scapegoat in the matter. The complainant has misused the provisions of criminal law to settle personal scores.\n\n5. That the Applicant is a respectable member of society with deep roots in the community and poses no flight risk whatsoever. He has permanent residence and family ties in the locality and shall remain available for trial proceedings as and when required by this Hon'ble Court.\n\n6. That the Applicant has no previous criminal antecedents and has never been involved in any criminal activity. His conduct has always been law-abiding and he enjoys good reputation in society. This is the first time he has been entangled in any legal proceedings.\n\n7. That the Applicant has been fully cooperating with the investigation and shall continue to do so. He has appeared before the investigating agency whenever called upon and has never attempted to obstruct the course of justice or tamper with evidence in any manner.\n\n8. That continued incarceration of the Applicant would be a violation of his fundamental right to life and personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India, especially when the allegations are false and motivated.\n\n9. That the investigation in the present case is pending and there is no likelihood of the Applicant tampering with evidence or influencing witnesses. The Applicant undertakes to abide by any conditions that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while granting bail.\n\n10. That considering the overall circumstances of the case, the false nature of allegations, absence of any criminal record, and the Applicant's willingness to cooperate with the investigation, the interest of justice would be served by granting bail to the Applicant."},{"section_id":"prayer","type":"template","content":"PRAYER\n\nIt is, therefore, most humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:\n\na) Grant Regular Bail to the Applicant, Rajan Kumar, in connection with FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15.03.2026, PS Kotwali, under Section 480 of BNSS, 2023, on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;\n\nb) Pass such other orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case, in the interest of justice.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness, the applicant shall ever pray.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"verification","type":"template","content":"VERIFICATION\n\nI, Rajan Kumar, the Applicant herein above named, do hereby verify that the contents of the above application are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and nothing material has been concealed therefrom.\n\nVerified at Patna on this _____ day of _________, 2026.\n\nDEPONENT\n\n\n_________________________\nRajan Kumar\n(Applicant)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"advocate_block","type":"template","content":"THROUGH:\n\n_________________________\nSmoke Test\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. ____________________\n\nPlace: Patna\nDate: 06 May 2026","alignment":"right"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

